meta-embedded-power-gateway
===========================

Custom Yocto layer for an Embedded Linux power monitoring gateway on Raspberry Pi.

This project demonstrates a complete embedded Linux workflow:

- Custom Yocto layer integration
- C-based power gateway application
- systemd service integration
- MQTT telemetry publishing
- PAC1944 power monitor integration
- Custom Linux kernel module for PAC1944
- Raspberry Pi target deployment

Current Architecture
====================

Raspberry Pi
    |
    |-- PAC1944 power monitor over I2C
    |
    |-- Custom kernel module: pac1944-driver
    |
    |-- Userspace gateway app: power-gateway
    |
    |-- MQTT telemetry output

Layer Structure
===============

conf/
    Yocto layer configuration

recipes-kernel/pac1944-driver/
    PAC1944 Linux kernel module recipe and source

recipes-power-gateway/power-gateway/
    C userspace application, systemd service, config file, and Yocto recipe

Build Integration
=================

Add this layer to your Yocto build:

    bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-embedded-power-gateway

Add packages to the image:

    IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " power-gateway pac1944-driver"

Build the image:

    bitbake core-image-minimal

Runtime Checks
==============

Check the service:

    systemctl status power-gateway

Check logs:

    journalctl -u power-gateway -f

Check kernel module:

    lsmod | grep pac1944
    dmesg | grep pac1944

Project Goal
============

The goal of this project is to build a production-style Embedded Linux gateway that combines Yocto image customization, kernel driver development, Device Tree integration, systemd service management, and MQTT-based telemetry.
